---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Subpage from '../../components/Subpage.astro';
import { en } from '../../i18n/en.ts';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site.ts';

const c = SITE.company;
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy | FILLCART LLC"
  description="Privacy policy for FILLCART LLC — controller, services used (GTM, Google Ads, HubSpot) and data-subject rights."
  path="/en/privacy"
  altPath="/datenschutz"
>
  <Subpage content={en} eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy">
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Last updated:</strong> July 2026. This policy describes the services currently used on
      this website. Further services (tracking, CRM) are loaded only once activated and only after
      consent — the policy will be extended accordingly at that point.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <div class="addr">
      {c.legalName}<br />
      {c.street}<br />
      {c.city}, {c.region} {c.postalCode}, {c.countryLabel}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${c.email}`}>{c.email}</a>
    </div>

    <h2>2. Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted by Vercel Inc. (340 S Lemon Ave #4133, Walnut, CA 91789, USA). When the
      site is accessed, Vercel processes technically necessary server log data (including IP address,
      timestamp, requested file) to deliver the site securely and reliably. The legal basis is our
      legitimate interest in secure operation (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). On the transfer to the US, see
      section 6.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Appointment booking (Google Calendar)</h2>
    <p>
      To book consultation slots we embed Google Calendar appointment scheduling (Google Ireland
      Limited, Ireland). When you use the booking widget, the data you enter (name, email, chosen
      slot) is transmitted to Google to confirm the appointment. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b)
      GDPR (pre-contractual measures / performance).
    </p>

    <h2>4. Contact &amp; audit request</h2>
    <p>
      When you use the request form or the contact channels (email, WhatsApp, phone), we process the
      information you submit solely to handle your request (Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR). Form requests
      are delivered to us by email; any form-delivery provider will be named here once activated.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Future services (only after consent)</h2>
    <p>
      Once reach and conversion measurement is activated (Google Tag Manager, Google Ads conversion
      tracking and remarketing by Google Ireland Limited) or HubSpot (HubSpot, Inc., USA) is embedded
      for forms and CRM, this happens only after your active consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR) via an
      upstream consent banner. Until then, no non-essential tags are loaded.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data transfer to the US</h2>
    <p>
      Some of the services used transfer data to the US (Art. 44 ff. GDPR). Transfers are based on
      Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) and/or the EU–US Data Privacy Framework. As the controller
      is itself a US LLC, particular diligence obligations apply here.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Objection (Art. 21 GDPR) and withdrawal of consent given</li>
      <li>Complaint to a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Retention: data is deleted as soon as the purpose of processing no longer applies and no statutory retention periods prevent it.</p>
  </Subpage>
</BaseLayout>
